# Anchored to this directory. Upstream wrote these unanchored, so patterns like
# `uadeutils.c` also matched src/frontends/common/uadeutils.c — real source that
# is a build input — and it silently never got committed. The UADE core then
# could not be built from a clean checkout.

/ossupport.c
/uadeipc.c
/uadeutils.c
/unixatomic.c
/sd-sound.[ch]
/gencpu
/uadecore
/compat.[ch]
/cpudefs.c
/cpuemu.c
/cpustbl.c
/cputbl.h
/build68k
